  "query_preview": "/Wednesday through Sunday/...\nIssued 349 AM MDT SUN OCT 4 2026\nThe ridge will remain in place through Thursday with highs\n10 to 20 degrees above normal. This will also keep skies mostly\nclear with light winds. On Friday, an upper level trough will \napproach the Pacific Northwest, increasing winds over the higher\nterrain. However, temperatures will remain warm ahead of a cold\nfront. The front will arrive on Saturday, cooling temperatures \nby about 15 degrees. Confidence on the evolution of the trough \ndecreases by Sunday, but additional cooling is likely as the \ntrough moves overhead. Ensembles indicate that subtropical \nmoisture will lift northeast across the Great Basin during this \nperiod and interact with the incoming trough, but favor keeping \nmost of the moisture east of our area. This will result in a \n20-40% chance of showers across eastern areas Saturday and \nSunday with a 10-20% chance elsewhere. Breezy winds will develop\nacross the area as the trough advances.",
